<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Shared test-spawn helper assembly (REFACTOR-3).

    Consolidates the process-spawn boilerplate that previously lived as
    near-duplicate copies in PsBash.Escalation.Tests/ProcessRunHelper.cs,
    PsBash.Canary.Tests/ModeRunner.cs, and
    PsBash.Differential.Tests/Oracle/BashOracleFixture.cs.

    A spawn-reliability fix (timeout, kill-tree, pipe-drain order, env
    canonicalisation, binary resolution) now lands once here and applies to
    every consuming suite — O(1) instead of O(N).

    DEPENDENCY-LIGHT BY DESIGN: the spawn primitive only needs System.*, so
    this assembly takes no repo ProjectReferences. That keeps it consumable by
    Escalation.Tests (refs Core+Shell+Host), Canary.Tests (refs Cmdlets), and
    Differential.Tests (refs Core) without forcing a common heavy dependency.

    The in-process SdkWorker path (Host.Tests) is intentionally NOT here: it is
    a different shape (in-process runspace, not Process.Start) and has a single
    consumer. Its dedup helper, HostWorkerFixture, lives in PsBash.Host.Tests
    next to PsBash.Host where SdkWorker is defined.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
